<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Ireland's Tullow plans exploration in India, B'desh.</title>
<headline>Ireland's Tullow plans exploration in India, B'desh.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Irish oil and gas producer and explorer Tullow Oil Plc said on Friday that it had the resources to fund an aggressive exploration programme, develop existing discoveries and expand into new areas.</p>
<p>Tullow said in a statement its exploration programme was currently being expanded into some promising new areas, with licences currently being finalised in India and Bangladesh.</p>
<p>&quot;Activity in the company over the next 12 months will be intense with exploration, development and production projects spread between established countries and new areas,&quot; managing director Aidan Heavey said.</p>
</text>
